1
00:00:05,620 --> 00:00:08,297
Today, you have proven
yourselves among the elite!

2
00:00:08,380 --> 00:00:11,057
And we, the Academy Knights, welcome you!

3
00:00:11,140 --> 00:00:14,657
As you know, I am the captain
of said knights, Loretta Kugrit.

4
00:00:14,740 --> 00:00:17,777
Some of you already know
my younger sister, Loretta.

5
00:00:17,860 --> 00:00:20,277
She happens to be a
first-year like yourselves!

6
00:00:20,360 --> 00:00:21,190
Oh, yeah!

7
00:00:21,273 --> 00:00:23,617
She's one half of
Miskler's minibus squadron!

8
00:00:23,700 --> 00:00:24,900
What is a minibus?

9
00:00:25,100 --> 00:00:28,512
I'm the vice-captain, Lambert
Aurousseau, at your service.

10
00:00:28,680 --> 00:00:29,897
It's a pleasure to meet you!

11
00:00:29,980 --> 00:00:32,980
And Lambert here is Lene's elder brother.

12
00:00:33,540 --> 00:00:36,317
Let's dive right into our first
order of business, shall we?

13
00:00:36,400 --> 00:00:38,341
Planning the Foundation Day Fair!

14
00:00:39,880 --> 00:00:41,360
The old FDF, huh?

15
00:00:41,600 --> 00:00:44,337
And what exactly are we knights
going to do for the big day?

16
00:00:44,420 --> 00:00:47,620
Well, we typically run a
cafe and serve customers.

17
00:00:47,820 --> 00:00:49,820
You'll be knights in dining armor!

18
00:00:50,200 --> 00:00:53,857
If I have to touch people's dirty
plates like some common servant girl,

19
00:00:53,940 --> 00:00:55,587
I am literally going to die.

20
00:00:55,800 --> 00:00:58,037
A regular cafe does sound a little boring.

21
00:00:58,120 --> 00:01:00,117
Maybe we could add some kind of theme.

22
00:01:00,200 --> 00:01:02,297
It's never a good sign
when he gets creative.

23
00:01:02,380 --> 00:01:04,086
A cafe does not need a theme.

24
00:01:04,200 --> 00:01:05,177
What do you think, Ray?

25
00:01:05,260 --> 00:01:06,201
Any suggestions?

26
00:01:06,300 --> 00:01:07,540
Uh, let me think.

27
00:01:07,960 --> 00:01:11,607
I guess we could go basic and
do a maid cafe or a butler cafe.

28
00:01:11,920 --> 00:01:14,817
Except there's nothing novel about
having a servant in this world.

29
00:01:14,900 --> 00:01:17,240
And I have no interest in sexy butlers.

30
00:01:17,540 --> 00:01:20,797
Although I would like to see Miss
Claire in a butler's uniform.

31
00:01:20,880 --> 00:01:22,460
Oh, now there's an idea.

32
00:01:23,280 --> 00:01:27,868
What if we draw people in with a gimmick
where the guys and girls swap styles?

33
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:30,840
Hold on, when you say styles,

34
00:01:31,120 --> 00:01:35,017
do you mean the ladies will dress
as butlers and we'll dress as maids?

35
00:01:35,100 --> 00:01:35,930
Exactly.

36
00:01:36,013 --> 00:01:40,797
The same basic cafe that we all know and
love, but with a delightfully quirky twist.

37
00:01:40,880 --> 00:01:42,351
I appreciate your vision,

38
00:01:42,500 --> 00:01:45,397
but would it be acceptable for
royals to participate in that?

39
00:01:45,480 --> 00:01:46,310
Hm?

40
00:01:46,393 --> 00:01:47,357
Why would it be a problem?

41
00:01:47,440 --> 00:01:49,080
Oh, where do I even begin?

42
00:01:49,400 --> 00:01:50,840
You're overthinking it.

43
00:01:51,040 --> 00:01:53,597
Besides, Rod's keen on the idea,
so let's let him have this one.

44
00:01:53,680 --> 00:01:54,897
Don't tell me you support this!

45
00:01:54,980 --> 00:01:57,717
I think I'd like to experiment
with dressing up as a girl.

46
00:01:57,800 --> 00:01:58,741
Sounds like fun.

47
00:01:58,920 --> 00:02:01,780
If Prince Hugh votes yes,
then I do too. Misha?

48
00:02:02,220 --> 00:02:03,960
Miss Claire in men's clothes?

49
00:02:04,160 --> 00:02:05,080
Good God, yes.

50
00:02:05,460 --> 00:02:07,117
I support you too, Prince Rai.

51
00:02:07,200 --> 00:02:09,937
You do not get a vote,
you lascivious creature.

52
00:02:10,020 --> 00:02:11,697
I should have known you'd do this.

53
00:02:11,780 --> 00:02:12,610
Miss Claire,

54
00:02:12,693 --> 00:02:16,497
don't you think that Prince Thane would
look adorable in a frilly maid uniform?

55
00:02:16,580 --> 00:02:18,240
Imagine the magnificence.

56
00:02:22,880 --> 00:02:23,717
Got him again.

57
00:02:23,800 --> 00:02:26,040
Well then, any objections?

58
00:02:26,520 --> 00:02:28,617
I'm 100 % against this idea.

59
00:02:28,700 --> 00:02:30,357
Voting has been closed, Captain!

60
00:02:30,440 --> 00:02:31,600
Yes!

61
00:02:32,100 --> 00:02:36,571
Then our festival project for this year
is officially a cross-dressing cafe!

62
00:02:53,800 --> 00:02:58,920
Yes, I know, no, I'm a pride
What you want? Say it again

63
00:02:59,800 --> 00:03:02,237
All I want, only you?

64
00:03:02,320 --> 00:03:04,380
Don't you know, you're a fool?

65
00:03:04,900 --> 00:03:08,757
You're a fool, you're a fool.

66
00:03:08,840 --> 00:03:11,637
You're a fool, you're a fool.

67
00:03:11,720 --> 00:03:13,426
You're a fool, you're a fool.

68
00:03:20,520 --> 00:03:23,697
Hey, you're a fool, you're a fool.

69
00:03:23,780 --> 00:03:26,457
I can't believe you,
you won't believe you!

70
00:03:26,540 --> 00:03:27,677
Or you won't believe me.

71
00:03:27,760 --> 00:03:28,597
I can't believe you, you won't believe me.

72
00:03:28,680 --> 00:03:32,620
I can't believe you, it's not an event.

73
00:03:35,080 --> 00:03:37,037
So I'll raise your hand.

74
00:03:37,120 --> 00:03:41,437
Now, the joy of happiness is equal.

75
00:03:41,520 --> 00:03:44,900
The secret is just one thing.

76
00:03:45,880 --> 00:03:47,757
Come from the heart.

77
00:03:47,840 --> 00:03:50,020
Raise your hand, let's do it.

78
00:03:50,760 --> 00:03:53,437
Raise your hand, if you're off.

79
00:03:53,520 --> 00:03:56,740
Rei-chan-han, more i-kai!

80
00:03:56,920 --> 00:03:59,460
Rei-chan-han, i-i-se-kai!

81
00:03:59,600 --> 00:04:01,718
I don't want to give up until I die!

82
00:04:02,720 --> 00:04:05,620
I love you, I love you!

83
00:04:23,520 --> 00:04:25,657
It's not too late to voice my opposition.

84
00:04:25,740 --> 00:04:26,570
Miss Claire.

85
00:04:27,660 --> 00:04:30,719
Thank you for being such a
good friend to my sister.

86
00:04:30,920 --> 00:04:34,160
Lene's spoken very highly
of you as well, Ray Taylor.

87
00:04:35,240 --> 00:04:36,617
Thank you, Master Lambert.

88
00:04:36,700 --> 00:04:38,857
I've heard that you're a
pretty good egg yourself.

89
00:04:38,940 --> 00:04:39,770
Really?

90
00:04:39,853 --> 00:04:41,401
You've heard of him before today?

91
00:04:41,500 --> 00:04:44,017
He's the magic tool specialist
who takes care of the

92
00:04:44,100 --> 00:04:46,737
Academy's maintenance and
inspection single-handedly.

93
00:04:46,820 --> 00:04:50,080
He's a renowned inventor
too, right, Master Lambert?

94
00:04:50,680 --> 00:04:53,092
I haven't done anything all that special.

95
00:04:53,520 --> 00:04:56,402
But I wondered if I might
ask a favor of you two.

96
00:04:57,720 --> 00:05:01,661
We've been noticing a lot more
conflicts between students recently.

97
00:05:01,960 --> 00:05:03,372
Now that you mention it,

98
00:05:03,460 --> 00:05:06,877
some of the commoners have been
behaving strangely as of late.

99
00:05:06,960 --> 00:05:07,790
Right.

100
00:05:07,873 --> 00:05:10,457
And a number of small fights
have broken out because of it.

101
00:05:10,540 --> 00:05:12,069
Goodness, how unfortunate.

102
00:05:12,420 --> 00:05:16,097
The captain and I have had our hands
full dealing with the altercations.

103
00:05:16,180 --> 00:05:18,637
I'm hoping you could investigate
some other matters for us.

104
00:05:18,720 --> 00:05:19,779
What do you think?

105
00:05:20,020 --> 00:05:21,357
Don't you know who I am?

106
00:05:21,440 --> 00:05:24,911
No matter what the occasion,
I shall rise to it flawlessly!

107
00:05:26,420 --> 00:05:29,400
I certainly appreciate it. Go on, then.

108
00:05:29,700 --> 00:05:32,406
What are the other matters
you need help with?

109
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:36,120
Well, you see, rumor has
it campus is haunted.

110
00:05:38,520 --> 00:05:39,350
Apparently,

111
00:05:39,433 --> 00:05:44,021
some students have reported seeing a
suspicious figure wandering the halls at night.

112
00:05:44,380 --> 00:05:46,060
Some see it in the stairway.

113
00:05:46,880 --> 00:05:48,040
Or in the kitchen.

114
00:05:49,160 --> 00:05:53,807
And when the students who were on night
patrol attempted to approach the figure

115
00:05:58,020 --> 00:06:02,785
Later on a wet spot in the shape of a
handprint was discovered on their shoulders

116
00:06:04,040 --> 00:06:07,117
Why Miss Claire you're looking
a little pale over there

117
00:06:07,200 --> 00:06:10,777
could it be that you're
afraid of Not another word you

118
00:06:10,860 --> 00:06:14,777
goblin I fear nothing do you
hear me oh my it seems I've

119
00:06:14,860 --> 00:06:17,737
hit a sore spot would you
prefer to do a different task?

120
00:06:17,820 --> 00:06:19,657
I mean, we've got cafe prep to do!

121
00:06:19,740 --> 00:06:21,277
But if the kitchen is full of coolies?

122
00:06:21,360 --> 00:06:22,977
then that might be out, too.

123
00:06:23,060 --> 00:06:25,277
Well, so far, there have
only been sightings.

124
00:06:25,360 --> 00:06:27,184
It hasn't damaged anything yet.

125
00:06:27,400 --> 00:06:29,757
I'll just cover our eyes
if we see something.

126
00:06:29,840 --> 00:06:32,997
It is the Knight's solemn duty to
protect the Academy's students!

127
00:06:33,080 --> 00:06:35,997
It would be wrong to ignore any
disturbance, however trivial!

128
00:06:36,080 --> 00:06:38,256
Oh, what are you saying, Miss Claire?

129
00:06:38,600 --> 00:06:40,940
I am saying, let the vile specter come!

130
00:06:41,140 --> 00:06:44,964
I shall be the most noble ghost
hunter this world has ever known!

131
00:06:45,520 --> 00:06:49,400
And that is how my spooktacular
evening with Ms. Claire began.

132
00:07:03,060 --> 00:07:05,060
Target location has been reached.

133
00:07:05,700 --> 00:07:08,288
I'll go scope out the
prep room in the back.

134
00:07:08,600 --> 00:07:11,277
Can you stay here where it's
light and keep a lookout?

135
00:07:11,360 --> 00:07:13,857
Did you really just get
me an order, commoner?

136
00:07:13,940 --> 00:07:14,770
Sorry.

137
00:07:14,853 --> 00:07:16,694
You can go to the back room if you want

138
00:07:19,280 --> 00:07:23,037
No, I shall let it go this time, but
don't you dare let it happen again.

139
00:07:23,120 --> 00:07:24,980
All right, let's bust a ghost

140
00:07:38,440 --> 00:07:41,460
Ghosts are real ghosts are not real

141
00:07:44,420 --> 00:07:45,917
Of course they aren't real.

142
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:46,830
How absurd.

143
00:07:46,913 --> 00:07:49,801
Those foolish students
must have been half asleep.

144
00:07:51,820 --> 00:07:52,677
Are you okay?

145
00:07:52,760 --> 00:07:53,590
What happened?

146
00:07:53,900 --> 00:07:56,820
Look, my hand is covered in goop. Hmm.

147
00:07:57,820 --> 00:07:58,650
Oh, you're right.

148
00:07:58,733 --> 00:08:00,537
It looks like some kind of gelatin.

149
00:08:00,620 --> 00:08:01,450
What is it?

150
00:08:01,760 --> 00:08:03,377
Have I been attacked by a ghost?

151
00:08:03,460 --> 00:08:07,557
Probably nothing to worry about, but
we'll send it in for analysis to be sure.

152
00:08:07,640 --> 00:08:09,640
I was covered in something sticky.

153
00:08:09,760 --> 00:08:10,817
Why are you so calm?

154
00:08:10,900 --> 00:08:12,517
You'll be fine with some soap and water.

155
00:08:12,600 --> 00:08:16,541
Why don't you just hang out here
until I finish exploring the back?

156
00:08:18,540 --> 00:08:20,997
Those presumptuous
academy knights forcing me

157
00:08:21,080 --> 00:08:23,727
to spend the night here
like a scullery maid!

158
00:08:23,820 --> 00:08:25,560
What if ghosts are real?

159
00:08:25,760 --> 00:08:27,819
What if there's one here right now?

160
00:08:28,060 --> 00:08:29,320
Hello, Miss Squire!

161
00:08:32,420 --> 00:08:33,820
For you, madame.

162
00:08:34,700 --> 00:08:36,288
Wait, what am I looking at?

163
00:08:36,480 --> 00:08:38,420
It is good fondant au chocolat.

164
00:08:38,640 --> 00:08:41,417
It's sort of like a chocolate
cake, but better and gooier.

165
00:08:41,500 --> 00:08:43,397
But where on earth did you get this?

166
00:08:43,480 --> 00:08:47,177
You really expect me to believe you managed
to acquire a cake made from chocolate?

167
00:08:47,260 --> 00:08:48,877
Brumet's exclusive new confection?

168
00:08:48,960 --> 00:08:49,837
Explain yourself!

169
00:08:49,920 --> 00:08:51,497
You could get bogged down in the details,

170
00:08:51,580 --> 00:08:54,933
or you could just take a bite
and tell me what you think.

171
00:08:55,060 --> 00:08:55,890
Fine.

172
00:08:55,973 --> 00:08:59,348
I'll have you know I'm not easily
impressed, but I'll try it.

173
00:09:02,660 --> 00:09:03,542
It's delicious!

174
00:09:04,300 --> 00:09:06,777
The cake is so rich in chocolate flavor,

175
00:09:06,860 --> 00:09:09,957
and more chocolate oozes
out with every bite.

176
00:09:10,040 --> 00:09:12,420
Why, it's positively heavenly!

177
00:09:13,120 --> 00:09:16,355
Commoner, I must meet the
patissier who concocted this!

178
00:09:17,260 --> 00:09:18,940
Wait, hold on.

179
00:09:19,380 --> 00:09:21,540
Are you saying you made this cake?

180
00:09:22,640 --> 00:09:26,497
I've been coming up with all kinds of
scrumptious recipes to make for you.

181
00:09:26,580 --> 00:09:28,757
How do you find time
to fiddle about in the

182
00:09:28,840 --> 00:09:31,252
kitchen when you're always at my service?

183
00:09:32,080 --> 00:09:32,910
Wait,

184
00:09:32,993 --> 00:09:35,919
a suspicious figure that
shows up night after night,

185
00:09:36,020 --> 00:09:38,777
wandering the halls, haunting the kitchen!

186
00:09:38,860 --> 00:09:40,100
Don't tell me!

187
00:09:40,440 --> 00:09:42,377
You're the ghost we've been hunting for!

188
00:09:42,460 --> 00:09:43,780
Am I spooky enough?

189
00:09:45,620 --> 00:09:48,157
Why didn't you tell me
instead of letting me suffer?!

190
00:09:48,240 --> 00:09:49,711
I wanted to surprise you!

191
00:09:50,220 --> 00:09:51,050
Dede!

192
00:09:51,133 --> 00:09:53,767
I made his food in a
nice cozy spot to sleep.

193
00:09:54,060 --> 00:09:55,580
She's been planning it.

194
00:09:55,820 --> 00:09:56,817
Wait, what is this?

195
00:09:56,900 --> 00:09:58,317
Why did you only bring one cot?

196
00:09:58,400 --> 00:09:59,929
It's like a slumber party!

197
00:10:00,700 --> 00:10:03,177
Things have taken a
turn for the ridiculous.

198
00:10:03,260 --> 00:10:05,613
I'm leaving as soon as I finish my cake.

199
00:10:06,180 --> 00:10:09,057
Aw, you're really not gonna
spend the night with me?

200
00:10:09,140 --> 00:10:10,240
Of course I'm not!

201
00:10:10,380 --> 00:10:12,977
And we've already solved the
mystery of the fake ghost!

202
00:10:13,060 --> 00:10:13,890
Huh?

203
00:10:13,973 --> 00:10:16,160
But, um, what about
the handprints, though?

204
00:10:16,320 --> 00:10:18,908
I genuinely don't know
where they came from.

205
00:10:20,240 --> 00:10:21,120
Enough games!

206
00:10:21,320 --> 00:10:22,217
I'm not a fool!

207
00:10:22,300 --> 00:10:24,137
And I won't fall for your tricks again!

208
00:10:24,220 --> 00:10:26,480
I'm not kidding, though. Oh, stop it!

209
00:10:26,640 --> 00:10:29,480
I'm going back to my
room! Wait! Miss Claire!

210
00:10:35,340 --> 00:10:37,200
Assistant, go save me!

211
00:10:39,280 --> 00:10:40,540
Oh, Ray Lair!

212
00:10:41,420 --> 00:10:42,980
What? Ray Lair?

213
00:10:45,280 --> 00:10:46,520
Whatcha doing, girl?

214
00:10:46,720 --> 00:10:48,073
Did you follow me here?

215
00:10:48,480 --> 00:10:50,180
Wait, the handprint.

216
00:10:50,360 --> 00:10:52,840
How long that was... her? Oh yeah!

217
00:10:53,280 --> 00:10:55,280
Ray Lair's on a transforming kick!

218
00:10:59,340 --> 00:11:00,740
I am done. Goodbye.

219
00:11:01,160 --> 00:11:03,200
Aww, we were gonna cuddle!

220
00:11:17,940 --> 00:11:20,411
So, um, does this mean you're not leaving?

221
00:11:20,520 --> 00:11:23,760
I would have, but I'm exhausted
from all your nonsense.

222
00:11:24,360 --> 00:11:25,190
What's wrong?

223
00:11:25,273 --> 00:11:26,317
Don't just stand there.

224
00:11:26,400 --> 00:11:27,929
Are you getting in or not?

225
00:11:33,260 --> 00:11:34,090
It's cold.

226
00:11:34,173 --> 00:11:36,020
Could you scoot a little closer?

227
00:11:36,280 --> 00:11:39,540
Touch me, and I will smother
you in your sleep! Hurry!

228
00:11:40,760 --> 00:11:41,600
Try there!

229
00:11:41,920 --> 00:11:43,626
You have to stay on the side!

230
00:11:50,760 --> 00:11:52,420
Mother? Hello?

231
00:11:52,980 --> 00:11:54,180
Where are you?

232
00:11:54,620 --> 00:11:57,020
I don't want to sleep by myself tonight!

233
00:11:57,480 --> 00:11:59,140
I feel so frightened!

234
00:12:00,100 --> 00:12:01,280
Mother, please!

235
00:12:05,380 --> 00:12:06,480
Ms. Clare?

236
00:12:08,800 --> 00:12:09,630
Lene?

237
00:12:09,860 --> 00:12:13,117
I'm sorry, but your mother
won't be returning home tonight.

238
00:12:13,200 --> 00:12:16,200
And the Master is still
busy with work, I'm afraid.

239
00:12:18,080 --> 00:12:18,910
Oh...

240
00:12:20,380 --> 00:12:21,210
No!

241
00:12:21,293 --> 00:12:22,560
I don't want you to leave!

242
00:12:22,720 --> 00:12:25,197
You and Father have to
stay with me always!

243
00:12:25,280 --> 00:12:29,162
I'm so sorry, my love, but it's
past time for us to be on our way.

244
00:12:29,760 --> 00:12:31,160
But you can't go now!

245
00:12:31,280 --> 00:12:32,217
Today's my birthday!

246
00:12:32,300 --> 00:12:35,006
What's so important that
you have to leave me?

247
00:12:35,960 --> 00:12:37,040
Oh, Claire.

248
00:12:37,440 --> 00:12:38,440
Come now, Claire.

249
00:12:38,840 --> 00:12:40,487
Show your mother some grace.

250
00:12:40,780 --> 00:12:44,340
As nobles, we must put our
duties before all else.

251
00:12:48,680 --> 00:12:53,780
I know, but you always tell me to be
patient when you leave, and I have been.

252
00:12:54,040 --> 00:12:58,700
I've become really good at it, so
I thought maybe just this once.

253
00:12:59,860 --> 00:13:01,117
I'm sorry, dear.

254
00:13:01,200 --> 00:13:02,380
Truly, I am.

255
00:13:02,620 --> 00:13:04,973
But I'll make this up to you, I promise.

256
00:13:05,560 --> 00:13:06,390
Oh, I know.

257
00:13:06,500 --> 00:13:08,853
I'll buy you a special birthday present.

258
00:13:08,960 --> 00:13:10,901
You can choose whatever you want.

259
00:13:11,200 --> 00:13:12,376
What would you like?

260
00:13:12,680 --> 00:13:14,000
No, forget it!

261
00:13:14,120 --> 00:13:15,520
I don't want a present!

262
00:13:15,740 --> 00:13:17,420
I hate you! Claire!

263
00:13:23,820 --> 00:13:24,650
Amelia.

264
00:13:45,020 --> 00:13:47,580
A very happy birthday to you, Ms. Clare.

265
00:13:47,740 --> 00:13:49,564
May there be many more to come.

266
00:13:51,300 --> 00:13:52,340
This is for you.

267
00:13:52,560 --> 00:13:55,325
We all work together to
pick something special.

268
00:14:00,340 --> 00:14:03,797
Wow it's pretty but I
think it might be too big

269
00:14:03,880 --> 00:14:06,897
for me to use right now
you may need some time to

270
00:14:06,980 --> 00:14:10,137
grow into it but until
that happens I think it

271
00:14:10,220 --> 00:14:13,280
might be nice if you used
it to brush Lady Melia's

272
00:14:16,320 --> 00:14:17,840
That's a great idea!

273
00:14:18,320 --> 00:14:19,820
I'm gonna do that!

274
00:14:22,500 --> 00:14:24,860
Now then, shall we sit down to dinner?

275
00:14:31,600 --> 00:14:33,840
Ms. Claire! Ms. Claire!

276
00:14:36,720 --> 00:14:38,860
I have terrible news, Ms. Claire!

277
00:14:39,080 --> 00:14:40,140
Please open up!

278
00:14:42,200 --> 00:14:43,030
What?

279
00:14:43,113 --> 00:14:44,497
Your parents were in a carriage accident.

280
00:14:44,580 --> 00:14:46,080
Lady Melia, what?

281
00:15:03,600 --> 00:15:07,160
Miss Claire, you should try
to at least eat something.

282
00:15:07,400 --> 00:15:09,341
I'm worried that you'll get sick.

283
00:15:17,360 --> 00:15:21,080
Maybe if I die, I'll
get to see Mother again.

284
00:15:21,640 --> 00:15:23,437
How could you say such a thing?

285
00:15:23,520 --> 00:15:26,108
Lady Melia would be so
sad if she heard you!

286
00:15:27,240 --> 00:15:31,520
Before she left, I told my
mother that I hated her.

287
00:15:34,760 --> 00:15:39,400
We were fighting, and that was
the last thing I ever said to her.

288
00:15:40,280 --> 00:15:42,100
Why did I say that?

289
00:15:42,500 --> 00:15:44,160
What's wrong with me?

290
00:15:45,720 --> 00:15:49,640
I didn't get to tell her that I was sorry.

291
00:15:58,200 --> 00:15:59,800
I'm sorry, Mother.

292
00:16:29,220 --> 00:16:30,980
Oh, I almost forgot.

293
00:16:31,160 --> 00:16:33,377
I talked with Master
Lambert for a bit yesterday.

294
00:16:33,460 --> 00:16:34,700
Oh, you did?

295
00:16:35,080 --> 00:16:37,000
Yeah, he's a stand-up gent.

296
00:16:37,260 --> 00:16:39,817
He's kind and reliable and very humble.

297
00:16:39,900 --> 00:16:41,577
even though he's super talented.

298
00:16:41,660 --> 00:16:42,660
He really is.

299
00:16:42,900 --> 00:16:44,897
And did you know, along with
his magic tool research,

300
00:16:44,980 --> 00:16:47,117
he's also learning how
monsters become familiars?

301
00:16:47,200 --> 00:16:49,788
They made him vice-captain
because of how...

302
00:16:52,580 --> 00:16:55,117
Anyway, I'm so proud
to call him my brother.

303
00:16:55,200 --> 00:16:56,477
Sure, who wouldn't be?

304
00:16:56,560 --> 00:17:00,257
So, would you mind helping us with
prep for the Foundation Day Fair?

305
00:17:00,340 --> 00:17:03,940
Well, I think Master Lambert
would appreciate it. Yeah?

306
00:17:08,780 --> 00:17:10,860
Oh, this looks quite delicious.

307
00:17:11,320 --> 00:17:14,617
So this is the top pick for our
menu at the Foundation Day Fair?

308
00:17:14,700 --> 00:17:16,700
Yep, go on and taste it.

309
00:17:17,120 --> 00:17:18,473
Thank you for the food.

310
00:17:22,780 --> 00:17:23,640
It's good.

311
00:17:23,840 --> 00:17:25,880
This flavor, it tastes familiar.

312
00:17:26,920 --> 00:17:28,280
Oh, I know what it is.

313
00:17:28,460 --> 00:17:29,872
This must be mayonnaise.

314
00:17:30,020 --> 00:17:32,617
It's the new sauce that was
just released by Brumet.

315
00:17:32,700 --> 00:17:33,530
So delicious.

316
00:17:33,940 --> 00:17:35,764
Right on the mail, Miss Claire.

317
00:17:36,100 --> 00:17:37,276
It's from Broom, eh?

318
00:17:37,500 --> 00:17:39,700
How did you get something like that?

319
00:17:40,720 --> 00:17:45,080
Uh, well, uh, I heard about it
and then tried making my own.

320
00:17:47,300 --> 00:17:48,900
Try these ones next, okay?

321
00:17:49,400 --> 00:17:52,237
Using limited ingredients
really makes the meat stand out.

322
00:17:52,320 --> 00:17:56,360
Yes, I must admit, you're quite
the chef for a lowly commoner. Hmm.

323
00:18:00,540 --> 00:18:02,677
Ray, may I ask you something? Hmm?

324
00:18:02,760 --> 00:18:07,197
You wouldn't happen to be the one supplying
all of these new recipes to Brumet now,

325
00:18:07,280 --> 00:18:08,110
would you?

326
00:18:09,180 --> 00:18:11,077
Because of the whole mayonnaise thing?

327
00:18:11,160 --> 00:18:11,990
That was just...

328
00:18:12,073 --> 00:18:12,903
You can't fool me.

329
00:18:12,986 --> 00:18:16,357
I know it's next to impossible to guess a
recipe like that after hearing about it.

330
00:18:16,440 --> 00:18:19,240
The ingredients, the texture, the taste.

331
00:18:19,520 --> 00:18:23,226
Why would it take a culinary
genius to get them all just right?

332
00:18:23,660 --> 00:18:24,677
Uh, oh, stop it!

333
00:18:24,760 --> 00:18:25,717
You're bothering me!

334
00:18:25,800 --> 00:18:27,317
Tell me about the meat, then.

335
00:18:27,400 --> 00:18:30,937
Is rare meat on sandwiches
a Brumet innovation as well?

336
00:18:31,020 --> 00:18:32,880
Oh, that wasn't just rare meat.

337
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:37,529
It's actually called rosé, and it looks
like that because the myoglobin is...

338
00:18:37,660 --> 00:18:38,600
Oh, crap.

339
00:18:38,900 --> 00:18:40,460
Caught by a true foodie.

340
00:18:40,780 --> 00:18:43,015
Might as well spill some of the beans.

341
00:18:43,540 --> 00:18:44,740
Okay, you're right.

342
00:18:44,960 --> 00:18:48,697
I've secretly been giving my recipes
to Brumet to put on their menu.

343
00:18:48,780 --> 00:18:52,637
It's common sense to utilize skills
from a previous life to turn a profit.

344
00:18:52,720 --> 00:18:57,397
Brumet is the only upscale restaurant in
this country, so the payoff was massive.

345
00:18:57,480 --> 00:19:00,598
Fun fact, chocolate was the
first recipe I sold them.

346
00:19:01,280 --> 00:19:05,037
But please, promise me that you'll
keep this between you and me.

347
00:19:05,120 --> 00:19:06,060
I don't get it.

348
00:19:06,280 --> 00:19:08,817
Being the Taliban, Brumet's
menu is impressive.

349
00:19:08,900 --> 00:19:09,730
Why hide it?

350
00:19:10,560 --> 00:19:12,580
I can't tell you all the details.

351
00:19:12,880 --> 00:19:14,704
Just know it's for Miss Claire.

352
00:19:15,540 --> 00:19:16,893
Wait, what do you mean?

353
00:19:17,340 --> 00:19:18,480
Afraid I can't say.

354
00:19:18,720 --> 00:19:19,897
Just please don't tell her.

355
00:19:19,980 --> 00:19:23,039
I mean, we all have a few
secrets, don't we, Lene?

356
00:19:27,600 --> 00:19:28,820
I suppose so.

357
00:19:29,360 --> 00:19:32,337
But in return, will you promise
to teach me one of your recipes?

358
00:19:32,420 --> 00:19:33,380
If you want.

359
00:19:33,940 --> 00:19:34,770
Yes.

360
00:19:34,853 --> 00:19:37,346
I want to make something
good for Miss Claire.

361
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:41,941
Okay, meet me here again tonight.

362
00:19:45,560 --> 00:19:48,207
So you decided to bring
Miss Claire with you.

363
00:19:48,700 --> 00:19:50,740
Did I interrupt your secret club?

364
00:19:51,220 --> 00:19:54,617
If you two are planning to make
something, then you are in luck.

365
00:19:54,700 --> 00:19:57,017
I'll lend you my palate as a taste tester.

366
00:19:57,100 --> 00:19:57,930
What the heck?

367
00:19:58,013 --> 00:19:59,637
I told you not to tell her anything!

368
00:19:59,720 --> 00:20:00,550
I'm sorry.

369
00:20:00,633 --> 00:20:02,080
I was just so excited.

370
00:20:02,800 --> 00:20:04,060
Nothing I can do now.

371
00:20:04,820 --> 00:20:05,780
Put this on.

372
00:20:06,020 --> 00:20:07,457
I think it's chilly at night.

373
00:20:07,540 --> 00:20:10,011
Let us know if you need something heavier.

374
00:20:13,340 --> 00:20:15,840
Hurry up and cook something. Okay!

375
00:20:22,620 --> 00:20:25,260
Tonight we have the crème brûlée.

376
00:20:34,220 --> 00:20:35,260
It's delicious!

377
00:20:35,660 --> 00:20:38,366
You've really outdone
yourself this time, Rei.

378
00:20:39,780 --> 00:20:42,080
It's even richer than regular custard.

379
00:20:42,200 --> 00:20:44,671
The caramelized sugar on top is exquisite!

380
00:20:45,560 --> 00:20:47,777
Would you mind getting me some tea, Lene?

381
00:20:47,860 --> 00:20:48,690
Coming up!

382
00:20:55,640 --> 00:20:56,540
Hey, Lene.

383
00:20:57,480 --> 00:20:58,360
For you.

384
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:04,480
Ray, is this a recipe for mammoth?

385
00:21:05,440 --> 00:21:07,616
Memorize it, and then ditch the note.

386
00:21:07,920 --> 00:21:08,880
It's insurance.

387
00:21:09,460 --> 00:21:10,290
Okay?

388
00:21:10,373 --> 00:21:14,180
I just really want you to have
this, in case you ever need it.

389
00:21:22,240 --> 00:21:26,260
I will need to sample this
again. What? You want another?

390
00:21:26,500 --> 00:21:28,257
Miss Claire, that's a lot of sugar.

391
00:21:28,340 --> 00:21:29,170
It's okay.

392
00:21:29,253 --> 00:21:32,709
I'd recommend whipping up another
batch for practice anyway.

393
00:21:38,460 --> 00:21:39,880
Are you okay?

394
00:21:40,200 --> 00:21:42,080
Yes, just burn myself a little.

395
00:21:50,180 --> 00:21:52,020
My, you're quite the healer.

396
00:21:52,180 --> 00:21:53,860
You two seem awfully close.

397
00:21:54,120 --> 00:21:56,061
Why, Miss Clara, are you jealous?

398
00:21:56,240 --> 00:21:57,657
Oh, I don't know what you're saying.

399
00:21:57,740 --> 00:22:00,877
What exactly do you think I'd be
jealous of, you impertinent insect?

400
00:22:00,960 --> 00:22:01,960
Here we go again.

401
00:22:02,680 --> 00:22:08,400
On days like this, I'm reminded that even
when nothing major happens, I'm so lucky.

402
00:22:09,900 --> 00:22:12,660
I just wish this happiness
could last forever.

403
00:22:13,700 --> 00:22:15,820
But I know better than that.

404
00:22:21,600 --> 00:22:24,620
Thank you so much.

405
00:22:52,100 --> 00:22:54,120
Thank you.

406
00:23:49,060 --> 00:23:52,560
You have to read this. Be
delicious. Be delicious.

407
00:23:53,040 --> 00:23:56,300
Love, love. Squee, squee. I love you. Huh!

408
00:23:56,640 --> 00:23:58,169
What in the world is this?

409
00:23:58,300 --> 00:24:00,277
It's the moment you've
all been waiting for!

410
00:24:00,360 --> 00:24:01,772
The Foundation Day Fair!
